<title>USA: NY Gov sees no progress with budget despite talks.</title>
<headline>NY Gov sees no progress with budget despite talks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Gov. George Pataki on Thursday said the state's approximately $64 billion budget, which was due on April 1, was stalled despite staff talks that continued during the legislature's spring break.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been no real progress on any issue concerning the budget at this point,&quot; Pataki told reporters in Albany.</p>
</text>
